{"causes": ["The ongoing Premyslid dynastic struggles for control of the Bohemian duchy created a climate of instability and frequent changes in leadership.", "The intervention of the Holy Roman Emperors, particularly Henry V, in Bohemian succession disputes provided external leverage for various claimants to the throne.", "The internal divisions and rivalries among the Bohemian nobility, such as the Vršovci, fueled plots and assassinations against ruling dukes."], "effects": ["Svatopluk's assassination directly contributed to the continued political instability and a protracted period of dynastic conflict within Bohemia.", "His brief reign led to the temporary return of Vladislav I to the Bohemian throne, further complicating the succession narrative.", "The violent end to his rule reinforced the perception of the Bohemian ducal seat as a highly contested and dangerous position."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "borivoj-ii-duke-of-bohemia", "sourceName": "Borivoj II, Duke of Bohemia", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "svatopluk-duke-of-bohemia", "targetName": "Svatopluk, Duke of Bohemia", "context": "Borivoj II's unpopularity and subsequent exile in 1107 created the opportunity for Svatopluk to seize the Bohemian throne."}, {"sourceSlug": "svatopluk-duke-of-bohemia", "sourceName": "Svatopluk, Duke of Bohemia", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "borivoj-ii-duke-of-bohemia", "targetName": "Borivoj II, Duke of Bohemia", "context": "Svatopluk assumed the ducal throne of Bohemia after deposing Borivoj II in 1107 with imperial backing."}, {"sourceSlug": "henry-v-holy-roman-emperor", "sourceName": "Henry V, Holy Roman Emperor", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "svatopluk-duke-of-bohemia", "targetName": "Svatopluk, Duke of Bohemia", "context": "Emperor Henry V's military and political support was crucial in Svatopluk's successful claim to the Bohemian ducal throne in 1107."}, {"sourceSlug": "svatopluk-duke-of-bohemia", "sourceName": "Svatopluk, Duke of Bohemia", "verb